{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Cancel Effects","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and the store’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all-or-nothing"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"cancel id","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" effect or the imperative "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method. Identity lives outside the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Choosing an id","anchor":"Choosing-an-id","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A cancel id is any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Return "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to tag the work, and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to stop it:"}]},{"code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Passing "},{"code":"cancelInFlight: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels any effect already running under the id "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:"}]},{"code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".queryChanged","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"Cancel from view or scene code","anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" directly:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace","text":"What it does not replace"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"text":" continuation should still release it — use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTaskCancellationHandler"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defer"},{"text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"else"}]},{"type":"text","text":" has to stop the effect early."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"How-to-Guides","title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"title":"Add a Version Killswitch","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","abstract":[{"text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Add Analytics","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancelEffects()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","title":"cancelEffects()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancelEffects"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/canceleffects()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels all in-flight effects."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","title":"Add iCloud Sync","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddPersistence":{"title":"Add Persistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin and the "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro — no hand-written "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" classes, database actors, or "},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closures.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","title":"cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancellable","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"type